    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute is escalated to a human reviewer. No money moves — the contested SGD 8.50 is held, not collected and not refunded.\n\nWhy escalation. The driver's statement of 11 Aug 2026 says 'PIE was closed, LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-02855-01 covers it.' That invokes the closure-exoneration clause POL-RD-03 and expressly cites advisory EV-ADVIS-02855-01. In this bundle that artifact has admissibility status MISSING, a null payload, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT and weight_multiplier 0.0, so it is absent from the pool (POL-GEN-02(3) narration: the ruling depends on EV-ADVIS-02855-01 at weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, and on its absence alone). POL-RD-10(5) makes an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact that is missing from the pool a mandatory escalation, and POL-RD-13(1) is explicit that while an uncited traffic excuse carries no weight under POL-RD-08 and does not escalate, a party who does cite the missing identifier is not saved by that rule — that case still escalates. The driver named the identifier, so the case escalates, and POL-GEN-03 makes that outcome terminal.\n\nWhat the merits would have been (for the reviewer's information, not a payment). The rider's figures are otherwise sound. EV-GPS-02855 is complete — 184 fixes at 10-second spacing, 100% coverage, max gap 0.0 s — so it is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c) and needs no independent corroboration. It measures 23.41 km against the booked optimal of 17.6 km on EV-TRIP-02855: an excess of 5.81 km (33.01%), which clears both POL-RD-01 gates (greater than 20% and greater than 0.8 km) but stays below the materiality thresholds, so no POL-RD-06 pattern check is triggered. Recomputing under POL-RD-02 on EV-FARE-02855 (fare model METERED; surge multiplier 1.0 read from the fare breakdown, not the trip record) gives ((3.80 + 0.75 x 17.6 + 0.28 x 23.8) x 1.0) + 0.80 = 24.4640 against charged_total 30.69, i.e. 6.2260 rounded up to SGD 6.25. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and 20.29% of charged_total, so it would have been a PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 6.25, not the SGD 8.50 claimed. The escalation displaces that outcome because the driver's cited-but-absent advisory must be reviewed by a person, not because the arithmetic is wrong.\n\nClaims answered. Accepted: the driver's escalation argument under POL-RD-10(5) and POL-RD-13(1); and, as far as it goes, the driver's fallback that the trace is unimpaired and the arithmetic yields SGD 6.25 — but that sum cannot issue against a terminal escalation. Also accepted: the rider's POL-RD-01/POL-RD-02 computation of SGD 6.25; its POL-RD-07 showing that the trace is unimpaired; its disclosing that EV-ADVIS-02855-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 with issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, so POL-RD-03 cannot run and no exoneration is available; and its point that rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 0 and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0, so no heightened corroboration burden applies under POL-RD-08. Rejected/outweighed: the rider's conclusion that a PARTIAL_REFUND should issue — it is outweighed by the driver's citation of the missing advisory, which triggers the mandatory, terminal escalation; and any suggestion that the driver's traffic excuse simply falls away, because POL-RD-13(1) turns on whether the identifier was cited and here it was. No repeat-deviation pattern is established (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d 0 against completed_trips_90d 278), so no POL-RD-06 FULL_REFUND uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arises; and no billing-integrity defect exists (no ERP lines, no airport surcharge), so no POL-RD-09(4) referral arises. Referrals is therefore empty.\n\nWhat would resolve it. The genuine LTA advisory for the Tampines Mall / PIE corridor covering 06:38–07:17 SGT on 11 Aug 2026 — the record behind EV-ADVIS-02855-01 — so that POL-RD-03 can be run: an advisory naming a road or segment the optimal route traverses, a validity window overlapping the time the trace shows the vehicle would have reached that segment (15-minute buffer each end), and a route that leaves the optimal corridor before the affected segment and rejoins it after.\n\nConfidence is 0.85: the escalation rests on the driver's citation in the counterparty statement (which carries no weight_multiplier and so does not cap confidence) rather than on any weighted artifact."
  },
